Modifications:
Copyright 2026 Danfocus
- Adapted for Nokia XG-040G-MD and Nokia XG-040G-MF (non-Wi-Fi Airoha AN7581 XGS-PON ONTs)
- Port mapping: lan4 configured as WAN, lan1–lan3 as LAN ports in br-lan
- Stripped eth0 (internal CPU QDMA1 conduit) from user-facing port status
- Completely removed MT7996 Wi-Fi monitoring (token buffers, TX stats, airtime calibration, wifi_stats)
- Added real-time SoC/CPU temperature monitoring (/sys/class/thermal/thermal_zone0/temp) to the CPU/NPU gauge
- Added wired client flow tracking (■ CLIENTS) in PPE terminal strictly tied to physical ports LAN 1–3 via bridge FDB (preventing WAN gateway and upstream devices on lan4 from appearing as clients), with IP/hostname resolution from DHCP leases and ARP neighbors
- Replaced raw devmem register operations with safe read_reg wrapper to prevent shell arithmetic syntax errors
- Added DTS lookup for NPU firmware name (/proc/device-tree/soc/npu@1e900000/firmware-name)
- Added caching for NPU reserved memory regions to eliminate repetitive dmesg calls
- Fixed double-echo arithmetic parsing bug in get_status for npu_cores, offload_bound, and offload_total
- Improved physical WAN interface error and traffic detection for virtual/PPPoE connections
- Fixed QDMA1/QDMA2 host CPU drops tracking in HW Buffer: included rx_cpu_drop (registers 0x1fb505a0/0x1fb515a0) alongside rx_hwf_drop, displaying cumulative drop counters so host CPU drops are not silently masked when deltas are zero
- Enhanced WAN Integrity monitoring: renamed card to WAN Integrity to clearly reflect scope and included interface packet drops (rx_dropped/tx_dropped) alongside PHY CRC/framing errors on physical and virtual interfaces
- Updated RPCD ACL definitions to grant access to thermal sensor and safe devmem reads
